# A whole-folder remove that RAISES when the host refuses, on node, Rust, Swift and Kotlin (term/compiler decision 021,
# the shape of point 1b). Answered WITHOUT awaiting, as [blocking.tree](blocking.tree) is.
#
# `remove-all` removes what is at a path and, for a folder, everything in it, as node's `fs.rm` with `recursive` and
# `force` does: nothing there is no refusal, a link is removed and never followed. Node's own steps, in its order: the
# path's `lstat` (a refusal other than ENOENT is raised, as fs.rm's option check raises it), then for a folder its
# `rmdir`, and only when that answers ENOTEMPTY, EEXIST or EPERM its entries (`scandir`), each removed the same way (a
# file by `unlink`), then the `rmdir` again. A refused `rmdir` of a folder that is not empty, under a read-only parent,
# raises at once and leaves its entries there, as node does.
#
# Any refusal raises `failure`, its note node's own message, worded once by [failure.tree](failure.tree): each binding
# answers the refusal's code name (empty when carried out), the step as node's `syscall` names it, the host's text,
# and the path the step named, which is the path given or an entry under it
# (`EACCES: permission denied, rmdir '/x/.base/@term/code/log'`).
#
# A new module, never a change to the absorbing call: `remove` of [directory.tree](directory.tree) stays total, as
# `make` stays beside [create.tree](create.tree)'s `make-folder` (decision 021 point 1b, ruling 1473).
#
# Browser: there is no file system there, so this module has no browser binding.

mark unstable

load @term/base/native/{platform}/file/remove
  find remove-path

load @term/base/file/failure
  find raise-file-failure

# what is at `path`, and for a folder everything in it. Nothing there is carried out
task remove-all
  take path, like text
  like void
  save raw
    call remove-path
      read path
  call raise-file-failure
    read raw
    read raw/3
